_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_

**Guard built‑in filter lookup against prototype keys.**

Line 264 and Line 716 use `tag in BUILT_IN_FILTERS`, which also matches prototype keys (e.g., `toString`, `__proto__`) and can yield non‑filter functions or incorrect matches for user tags. Use `hasOwnProperty` to ensure only real built‑ins are treated as such.

<details>
<summary>🔧 Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
-          if (tag in BUILT_IN_FILTERS) {
+          if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(BUILT_IN_FILTERS, tag)) {
             acc['built-in'].push(BUILT_IN_FILTERS[tag as keyof typeof BUILT_IN_FILTERS]);
           } else {
             acc.user.push(USER_TAG_FILTER(tag));
           }
```

```diff
-      if (tag in BUILT_IN_FILTERS) {
+      if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(BUILT_IN_FILTERS, tag)) {
         return BUILT_IN_FILTERS[tag as keyof typeof BUILT_IN_FILTERS];
       } else {
         return USER_TAG_FILTER(tag);
       }
```
</details>



Also applies to: 716-720

