_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_

**Missing `componentWillUnmount` and React state initialization.**

The `this.mounted` flag is set to `true` in `componentDidMount`, but it's never reset to `false` in `componentWillUnmount`. If the store's `onChange` callback fires after the component unmounts, `this.setState` will still be called (since `this.mounted` remains `true`), potentially causing a React warning or memory leak.

Additionally, `this.setState(newState)` is called in the store callback, but the component's `state` is never initialized. React class components should initialize `this.state` in the constructor when using `setState`.


<details>
<summary>🔧 Suggested fix</summary>

```diff
   constructor(props: {
     children: React.ReactNode;
     args: Record<string, unknown>;
     initFn: ModuleFn<SubAPI, SubState>;
     initOptions?: Partial<ModuleArgs>;
     initialStoryState?: Partial<State>;
   }) {
     super(props);
+    this.state = {};

     // Set up store.
     this.mounted = false;
     this.store = createTestingStore({} as State, (newState) => {
       if (this.mounted) {
         this.setState(newState);
       }
     });
```

And add:

```diff
   componentDidMount() {
     this.mounted = true;
   }

+  componentWillUnmount() {
+    this.mounted = false;
+  }
+
   render() {
```
</details>

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In `@code/core/src/manager/components/sidebar/TagsFilter.stories.tsx` around lines
37 - 52, The constructor sets this.mounted and creates this.store but never
initializes this.state, and componentDidMount flips this.mounted true without
any componentWillUnmount to reset it; initialize the component state in the
constructor (e.g., this.state = this.props.initialStoryState || {} / appropriate
State shape) so setState calls are valid, and add a componentWillUnmount
lifecycle that sets this.mounted = false (and if createTestingStore returns an
unsubscribe, call it there) to prevent setState after unmount; update the
methods referenced (constructor, componentDidMount, componentWillUnmount,
mounted, store, setState) accordingly.
```

</details>

